{
 "about": "The compressor of the effect rack of the Audio Unit (alone in the rack; osc A off, the noise oscillator plays samples of ours one-shot at 44.1 kHz, the rate of the renders: sines of both channels in quadrature, their level hypot(L, R) at every sample; a gain is the level of a render over the one of the dry render, the rack empty, dB). `output`: the dry output over the sample (the rack is before Main Vol); `levels`: dB of a sample, add 20 log10(output) for the level at the output. `single` (one band, a step of 1 kHz from -40 to -9 dB and back): `threshold` [knob, gain at -9 dB, gain at -40 dB] with the attack 1 ms and the release 1 s (the peak is read); `ratio` [ratio, gain at -9 dB] at the threshold knob 0.7; `attack` and `release` [ms of the knob, [ms after the step, gain]] (the release from the gain at 0); `fresh` the same at the knobs of a fresh one (threshold 0.7); `makeup` and `level` [knob, gain] with no compression (at -40 dB: the rack clips an output over full scale); `mix` [mix, gain]; `link` the gain of the left channel with the right one as loud, a quarter of it, silent; `highpass` [Hz, dB, degrees] with no compression. `multi` (three bands): `curves` by band (a sine of its `hz`) and knobs: the gain at each of `levels` held 0.6 s; `mono` the same on a sine of 220 Hz alike in both channels (its fundamental); `falls` [ms of the release, [ms after a step from 0 to -40 dB, gain]] of the mid (1 kHz) and the high (8 kHz) band; `rise` [ms of the attack knob, [ms after a step from -40 to 0 dB of 1 kHz, gain]]; `onset` a hit of 1 kHz at 0 dB and at -40 dB after a second of a tone at -72 dB, by Below: the gain at each of its first `samples`, then its `trace` [ms after it, gain]; `gaps` [seconds of a silence between two tones of 1 kHz at 0 dB, [ms after the second one starts, gain]] at Below 1; `crossover` the response [dB, degrees] at `frequencies` with no compression: all bands, each alone (the others at -24 dB), at a mix of a half, with the crossovers moved; scripts/renders/run.mjs --only=compressor",
